---
<Layout title="Data and code | OpenIE Research" description="Where each paper's results live in the public experiments and reference repositories.">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-white">Data and code</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The reproducible material for these studies lives in <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments">github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments</a> and companion repositories under <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev">github.com/openIE-dev</a> (<a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce">rce</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-vc">rce-vc</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null">deterministic-null</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai">lut-adapt-ai</a>): preregistrations with SHA-256 digests, scripts, Lean 4 proof packages, CAD/ECAD hardware files, results, receipts, a repository-wide <code>CHECKSUMS.sha256</code>, and pinned references for large corpora (<code>CORPORA.md</code>). Code is Apache-2.0 and data is CC BY 4.0. Energy labels: <code>est_j</code> is an analytical estimate, <code>reported_j</code> an operating-system or on-chip counter, and <code>measured_j</code> a meter reading on a named hardware rail. Physical current-shunt <code>measured_j</code> readings are filed in three studies: Metered Commit Gates records three KV260 (AMD Kria) INA260 rows (Section I.4.9: a seed freerun in watts, an inconclusive +0.0098 W / 98.0 pJ per seed cycle halt-versus-run delta, and 11,428 pJ per gate cycle on the gate fabric), and both the Satiation Benchmark Harness and The Communication Tool Avalanche (CTA-E4 and CTA-E5) record Texas Instruments INA238 (whole-board VIN, L1) and three-channel INA3221 (VDD_GPU, VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS, VIN_SYS_5V0, L2) shunt joules on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (shared host, with A2 single-window net placement attribution withheld per Falsifier 6). On-chip <code>reported_j</code> receipts (Apple Silicon IOReport / proc_pid_rusage, Linux x86-64 RAPL, and Windows 11 NVML) are filed for the Reality Code Engine, RCE-VC, RCE-JEPA (H2, H15, FormJEPA-v1, FormEBM-v2, and FormEBM-v3), RCE Compile (E4-Energy, E4-Prelude, and E5-Scale), Deterministic Null, the Satiation Benchmark Harness, The Communication Tool Avalanche (CTA-E1 to CTA-E5), Downward LUT6 Compilation, Writing a Game Once (GE-H1 and GE-H5), and "AI" Reads Human, while <code>measured_j</code> remains empty across all software-only and simulated hardware runs.</p>
    {groups.map((g) => (
      <section id={g.id} class="mt-10">
        {g.aliases.map((a) => <div id={a} aria-hidden="true"></div>)}
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-brand-white"><a href={g.paper}>{g.title}</a></h2>
        <table class="mt-3 w-full font-body text-sm text-brand-slate">
          <thead><tr><th class="text-left pr-4">Result</th><th class="text-left pr-4">Repository or artifact path</th><th class="text-left">Contents</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{g.rows.map(([r, p, c]) => (<tr><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{r}</td><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{p ? <a href={hrefOf(p)}><code>{labelOf(p)}</code></a> : 'n/a'}</td><td class="py-1 align-top">{c}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
    ))}
  </main>
</Layout>
